==Dutch==

===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|dum|nl}} {{term|lesschen|lang=dum}}, from a merger of two verbs:
* {{etyl|odt|nl}} {{term/t|odt|*leskan}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|nl}} {{term/t|gem-pro|*leskanan}}; class 5 strong, intransitive. Cognate with Old High German {{term|leskan|lang=goh}} (German {{term|löschen|lang=de}}).
* {{etyl|odt|nl}} {{term/t|odt|*lesken}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|nl}} {{term/t|gem-pro|*laskijanan}}; class 1 weak, causative of the first verb. Cognate with Old Saxon {{term|aleskian|lang=osx}}, Old High German {{term|lesken|lang=goh}} (German {{term|löschen|lang=de}}).

